cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these models, please cite this data set and the three references listed below (the paper that describes the cases, the method paper, and the dissertation)."
type: dataset
title: "EPIGRIDS Synthetic Electric Network Models"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/WISPO-POP/SyntheticElectricNetworkModels"
url: "https://electricgrids.engr.tamu.edu"
abstract: >-
  Seven entirely synthetic transmission network models of U.S. regions, from
  250 to 78,484 buses: the Eastern and Western interconnections, Texas,
  Florida, Michigan-Ohio-Indiana (folder Midwest), Wisconsin, and a 250-bus
  New England system with 12 operating points. Each case is a PowerWorld
  Simulator case with a one-line diagram, a MATPOWER case and a PSS/E raw data
  file. The models were developed in the US ARPA-E GRID DATA program
  (EPIGRIDS project, award DE-AR0000717), model no actual transmission line,
  and contain no CEII.
keywords:
  - synthetic power grid
  - transmission network
  - power flow
  - optimal power flow
  - test case
  - EPIGRIDS
